Sval: size the Picture-in-Picture toggle from the video's real size

A <video> without controls gets a new NoControlsPictureInPictureImpl
widget when it comes back from Picture-in-Picture. The widget starts from
its default reflowedDimensions, 300 by 150, and sizes the toggle from
those in init. resizevideocontrols, which would correct them, comes only
when the video's size changes, and a video back from Picture-in-Picture
keeps its size, so the toggle stays marked small-video. init measures the
video first (updateReflowedDimensions), as the reflow handler does.

diff --git a/toolkit/content/widgets/videocontrols.js b/toolkit/content/widgets/videocontrols.js
index cec4a857c6..51f175297d 100644
--- a/toolkit/content/widgets/videocontrols.js
+++ b/toolkit/content/widgets/videocontrols.js
@@ -3194,6 +3194,11 @@ this.NoControlsDesktopImplWidget = class {
           // not to show the Picture-in-Picture toggle now.
           //
           // [1]: https://www.w3.org/TR/html50/embedded-content-0.html#dom-media-have_metadata
+          //
+          // Sval: a widget made for a video already laid out, as one back
+          // from Picture-in-Picture, gets no resizevideocontrols until its
+          // size changes, so it measures the video before sizing the toggle.
+          this.updateReflowedDimensions();
           this.updatePictureInPictureToggleDisplay();
         }
 
